=== How to use ===
1. Register the Entra app and expose its application ID URI; use the app ID in webApplicationInfo.id. Resource-specific consent needs this block.
2. Implement the configuration page, then the side panel page and stage view, and use the Teams JavaScript library to detect the meeting context.
3. Request only the RSC permissions you need. Chat members can grant delegated permissions when they install the app; application permissions need an administrator or resource owner.
4. Upload the package, add the app to a scheduled meeting and test the side panel, the stage view and a join as anonymous guest.
5. If you do not need guests, set supportsAnonymousGuestUsers to false and test the experience for internal users only.

=== Common mistakes ===
- Using the team scope for a meeting-only tab. Chat-based meetings use groupChat.
- Declaring RSC permissions without webApplicationInfo.
- Requesting application permissions that your service does not need; administrators will push back.
- Allowing anonymous guests without checking what data the side panel shows to them.
- Setting supportsStreaming to true without a real RTMP streaming scenario; it advertises that the app can stream meeting audio and video.
